fact WorkItem(id: "WI-756", description: some(value: "Proof-path coverage for override-aware eq: verify (and test) that the direct prove_from_gamma sites decide eq over a CUSTOM-eq carrier semantically, not structurally. This is WI-573's recorded 'RESIDUAL / review Finding C', filed separately as WI-573 flagged it out of its own guarded-effect-discharge scope. BACKGROUND: WI-573's override gate lives in the typer's conjunct_refuted (typing.rs ~21503) and therefore covers ONLY the guard-refutation route (refute_guard, typing.rs:1156-1158). The other prove_from_gamma call sites do NOT pass through that gate: (1) typing.rs:5471 — WI-538 'proof .. by derivation' (Expr::Proof, tier-A inline proof over Gamma union KB); (2) typing.rs:21871 — WI-539 precondition_proved, the call-site 'requires' obligation; (3) proof_verify.rs:602 — WI-558 contract 'ensures' discharge. NOTE Finding C named only sites (1) and (3) using pre-drift line numbers ('typing.rs ~3669' is now 5471); site (2), precondition_proved, was MISSED and must be included — it is the exact positive dual of precondition_refuted (typing.rs:21893), which DOES route through the gated conjunct_refuted, so the two polarities are asymmetric today and that asymmetry is itself worth asserting on. POLARITY OF THE RISK, which differs from WI-573's: the guarded-effect hazard was an unsound REFUTATION dropping an effect that should stay; here the hazard is an unsound PROOF — a precondition deemed satisfied, or an 'ensures' conjunct deemed derivable, on a structural eq verdict the carrier's own eq would contradict. CURRENT BELIEF (must be confirmed, not assumed): the gap appears to have closed INDIRECTLY when WI-616 made eq/neq semantic (BuiltinTag::SemEq/SemNeq -> sem_eq_core, resolve.rs:4010), since all four sites resolve THROUGH the resolver and so inherit its dispatch/delay discipline rather than a typer gate. If that holds, this ticket is characterization-and-regression work, not a fix. If it does NOT hold on some path, it is a live soundness bug in the WI-538/WI-539/WI-558 proof paths and should be fixed here. THE REAL GAP TODAY IS TEST COVERAGE: nothing exercises a custom-eq carrier on ANY proof path — none of WI-538/WI-539/WI-558 carry acceptance criteria mentioning one, and wi573_eq_override_discharge_test covers only guarded effects. Note also that WI-621 refactored precondition_proved/precondition_refuted/conjunct_refuted/guarded_atom_refuted to thread Value end-to-end but changed no eq semantics. Acceptance: for EACH of the three sites, a test with a carrier whose eq override DISAGREES with structural equality (the CUSTOM_EQ_TRUE_PRELUDE / STRUCTURAL_EQ_PRELUDE fixture pattern in tests/include/wi573_eq_override_discharge_test.rs) asserts the override decides — a 'proof by derivation', a call-site requires, and a contract ensures each resolve per the carrier's eq, NOT structurally; a non-ground or buried-override operand stays UNPROVED (definite_only maps the resolver's Delay to unproven — the obligation default) rather than being proved structurally; any path found deciding structurally is FIXED, not documented; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)

